   "text": "use broader channels and that's why B2C channels like Instagram are focused on more broader targeting. Wherein B2B channels like LinkedIn are focused on more precise targeting. You can target by company, by sales, or by their job profile, by their seniority, location, and multiple other filters. And the fourth thing is what is the consideration time in your product? Does your buyer decide in 5 seconds as with an impulse cosmetic purchase, let's say for Zoko or does it take 30 to 90 days like with a B2B software purchase for a customer like for Clairo? Now, this changes everything about what the channel has to do because let's say if it is an impulse purchase channel, it needs to convert on the spot. A considered purchase channel needs to nurture the lead and your prospect. Now, understand the same channel cannot do both the things well. Suppose if there's a billboard that works for a soap company might fail for an enterprise software company. So, when you consider all these 4 dimensions, plus the 6 channel properties that we learned about, it will give you 10 points of evaluation and here is the fit equation as a matrix that you can see. And then I want you to think of your growth budget as a sheet with rows for channels and columns for the product types or the dimensions that we exactly talked about. Now, across the top you can see 6 product types. B2B, low ACV. ACV we have already discussed, average contract value or annual contract value."
