   "lectureId": "IBM-M07-L04",
   "title": "Understanding the FPO Journey",
   "text": "So, many FPOs find it easier to be in the input business, become a conduit for the industry to sell to the farmers seeds and fertilizers, which is also good because as an FPO you have more bargaining power. But the real challenge comes in accessing the markets, and if you're able to get access to the markets and get good price from them, then your income will get more and more. There is price volatility, there is climate change, and there are a lot of production-related issues which are big challenges in front of the FPOs. Farmers in developed countries use commodity futures to get a sense of pricing. These are financial instruments which enable you to take some positions to reduce your risk. You get a sense of prices and you can say, \"Okay, after a year, what will be the rice prices in the marketplace?\" India is gradually getting there. It allows for a handful of commodities in the futures market, and there are about 200 FPOs who took position in the NCDEX, which is the commodity exchange market for agricultural products. I encourage you to look at the literature, look at something about NCDEX and how farmers can take positions in these future markets to cover their risk, but that is not something that I am going to cover in this particular course."
